        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0644" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg630"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[506]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McKeon, district
                        attorney, to Mr. Gushing, Attorney-General.</hi></head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southern District of New
                            York,<lb/>United States District Attorney’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1855-12-26"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 26, 1855</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A warrant has been issued by George W.
                    Morton, esq., United States commissioner, against Parker H. French, charged with
                    an offense against the laws of the United States, recently committed. Mr. French
                    claims to be a diplomatic representative of the state of Nicaragua, and the
                    offense charged against him was committed by him since assuming such character.
                    I have to request to be informed of the President’s directions as to whether
                    said warrant should be executed.</p>
                <p>I am, with high respect, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN McKEON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States District
                            Attorney.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caleb Cushing</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
